      "summaries": {
        "en": "NotebookLM-py is an unofficial Python API wrapper for Google's NotebookLM, enabling developers to programmatically access this AI-powered research assistant. It provides structured access to NotebookLM's core capabilities—document analysis, conversational Q&A, and source-based reasoning—through clean Python interfaces. Developers can integrate it into automated workflows, build custom research tools, or create applications that leverage NotebookLM's document-aware AI for tasks like content summarization, knowledge extraction, or interactive learning systems.",
        "zh": "NotebookLM-py 是 Google NotebookLM 的非官方 Python API 封装，让开发者能够通过代码调用这个基于文档的 AI 研究助手。它通过简洁的 Python 接口，提供了对 NotebookLM 核心功能的程序化访问，包括文档分析、对话式问答和基于来源的推理。开发者可以将其集成到自动化工作流中，构建定制化的研究工具，或开发利用 NotebookLM 文档感知能力的应用，例如内容摘要、知识提取或交互式学习系统，从而扩展 AI 辅助研究的可能性。",
        "es": "NotebookLM-py is an unofficial Python API wrapper for Google's NotebookLM, enabling developers to programmatically access this AI-powered research assistant. It provides structured access to NotebookLM's core capabilities—document analysis, conversational Q&A, and source-based reasoning—through clean Python interfaces. Developers can integrate it into automated workflows, build custom research tools, or create applications that leverage NotebookLM's document-aware AI for tasks like content summarization, knowledge extraction, or interactive learning systems.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "notebooklm-py stands out for ai-automation, api, and audio-overview in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "NotebookLM-py is an unofficial Python API wrapper for Google's NotebookLM, enabling developers to programmatically access this AI-powered research assistant. It provides structured access to NotebookLM's core capabilities—document analysis, conversational Q&A, and source-based reasoning—through clean Python interfaces. Developers can integrate it into automated workflows, build custom research tools, or create applications that leverage NotebookLM's document-aware AI for tasks like content summarization, knowledge extraction, or interactive learning systems.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/teng-lin/notebooklm-py for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
